  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Arithmetic of hyperbolic manifolds (Neumann–Reid) — survey of arithmetic Kleinian groups: an arithmetic M = H³/Γ is determined up to commensurability by its invariant trace field and quaternion…\n\n**Arithmetic of Hyperbolic Manifolds** — Walter D. Neumann and Alan W. Reid. Survey.\n\nHyperbolic 3-manifolds here are complete orientable finite-volume quotients H³/Γ with Γ ⊂ PSL₂ℂ a Kleinian group. The arithmetic ones form a more tractable subclass because arithmetic invariants are available: an arithmetic M is determined up to commensurability by its defining field k (a number field with exactly one complex place) together with a quaternion algebra over k.\n\nCovers the invariant trace field, the invariant quaternion algebra, commensurability classes, and the identification of arithmetic manifolds among all hyperbolic ones.\n\n**Why it may bear here.** The invariant trace field and quaternion algebra are the arithmetic side of the same hyperbolic-volume objects this corpus uses geometrically (Vol(4₁), cusp shapes, the Bloch-group material). Relevance is a prior, not a verdict — no claim is made that a specific result is needed.",
      "lang": "en",
